--- kaiju-mkbwt -
-a 	alphabet, ending with the terminator, or DNA, RNA or protein
-c 	the sequence is read case sensitive
-e 	exponent for suffix array checkpoints (one every 2^e points)
-h 	print a summary of the options and arguments
-l 	length of the sequence in millions of letters, when reading from stdin
-n 	number of threads
-o 	name of the output (several files with different extensions; default: the input's name)
-r 	reverse complement sequence
-s 	the termination symbols sort as reverse sequences (more compressible BWT)
-t 	terminating symbol (only used for debugging)
--- kaiju-mkbwt -a 
DNA 
RNA 
protein 
